title: Typed numbers stick
intro: Typing into a number field in the Inspector now changes the component.
project: Platformer | Number Fields

chapter: Typing a number | The Inspector's number fields
select: Player
say: Typing into the Inspector's plain number fields used to look like it worked, then quietly change nothing. Watch the jump height.
explain: field:PlatformerMovement.JumpHeight | Jump Height | Here's the player's jump height.
set: PlatformerMovement.JumpHeight = 6
say: Six, and this time it's really six. Let's prove it in the game.
play
wait: 0.5
tap: Space
wait: 1.5
say: That's a much bigger jump than the template's.
stop

chapter: Every kind of number | Whole numbers and decimals
say: Whole numbers work the same way. One air jump gives the player a double jump.
set: PlatformerMovement.AirJumps = 1
explain: field:PlatformerMovement.AirJumps | Air Jumps | Air Jumps is a whole number, and it sticks too.
say: Vectors, like Position, always worked. Now every number in the Inspector does.
